        "heading": "Intersensory Evidence",
        "body": "The intersensory findings provide a clear starting case. When visual word cues instructed participants to attend audition, parieto-occipital 8–14 Hz activity increased before the compound audiovisual target. Because fixation was maintained and the target had not yet appeared, this preparatory alpha increase supports anticipatory suppression of visual processing during auditory attention.",
        "grounding_claim_ids": [
