      },
      {
        "heading": "Spatial And Retinotopic Bias",
        "body": "The spatial attention evidence makes the suppression account more anatomically specific. In instructional cueing tasks, uncued locations never require a response, so they are genuine distracter sources. Alpha increases over occipital cortex ipsilateral to the attended side, matching the cortical territory expected to represent the ignored hemifield and shifting with retinotopic task demands.",
