{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p '/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/runs/run-20260426T111459Z--lhudn2ntw8/semantic' && cat > '/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/runs/run-20260426T111459Z--lhudn2ntw8/semantic/topic_generation.json' <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"topics\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-attentional-gating-and-sensory-suppression\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Attentional Gating and Sensory Suppression\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"Selective attention can be framed as a family of gating mechanisms that improve behavior by prioritizing relevant inputs and suppressing distracting ones.\\\",\n        \\\"Alpha-band evidence supports an active-suppression account: alpha power rises in cortical regions processing irrelevant visual, auditory, tactile, spatial, feature-based, or intersensory information, and stronger alpha is linked to weaker perceptual detection.\\\",\n        \\\"Mindfulness evidence provides a behavioral counterpart: training changes separable attention subsystems rather than producing a single global attention benefit, with MBSR improving endogenous orienting and intensive retreat experience altering alerting-related readiness.\\\",\n        \\\"The cross-source synthesis is strongest at the level of attention as selective control; the available evidence does not show that mindfulness training causes alpha-band suppression changes.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-alpha-band-oscillations-can-be-actively-invoked-in-cortical-regions-that-process--09466b39d396\\\",\n        \\\"claim-instructional-cuing-paradigms-distinguish-distracter-suppression-from-probabilis--af0b5b81b7e7\\\",\n        \\\"claim-in-intersensory-attention-tasks-attending-to-audition-increases-8-14-hz-parieto--6ff6ff285662\\\",\n        \\\"claim-during-visual-spatial-attention-alpha-band-power-increases-over-occipital-cortex--09a99b87f400\\\",\n        \\\"claim-feature-based-visual-attention-increases-alpha-power-in-dorsal-or-ventral-stream--0c7646ad3b93\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alpha-mediated-biasing-extends-beyond-vision-appearing-in-auditory-and-tactile-s--2cd546facc83\\\",\n        \\\"claim-sustained-focal-alpha-increases-above-pre-cue-baseline-during-rapid-bilateral-st--8699d621dccc\\\",\n        \\\"claim-higher-naturally-occurring-or-experimentally-induced-alpha-power-reduces-visual--3884cfa09119\\\",\n        \\\"claim-attention-related-alpha-modulation-appears-primarily-controlled-by-cortico-corti--1eb91088cf2b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-mindfulness-training-can-improve-attention-related-behavior-by-changing-specific--f9e8e6ee54d7\\\",\n        \\\"claim-an-8-week-mindfulness-based-stress-reduction-course-improves-endogenous-orientin--f7bde69b7431\\\",\n        \\\"claim-a-1-month-intensive-mindfulness-retreat-among-previously-experienced-meditators--cd2a814c579a\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-attention-network-test-separates-alerting-orienting-and-conflict-monitoring--08b2302acb19\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-attentional-effects-should-be-treated-as-preliminary-because-the-study-used--8a181621f4d7\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-03-the-role-of-alpha-band-brain-oscillations-as-a-sensory-suppression-mechanism-dur-w2005105933--7b6b7d5bc8b9\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-cortical-network-organization-and-conscious-access\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Cortical Network Organization and Conscious Access\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"Across the sources, cortical organization matters both for conscious experience and for selective attention, but the claims operate at different explanatory levels.\\\",\n        \\\"Information integration theory argues that consciousness depends on complexes with high integrated information, especially distributed thalamocortical systems combining functional specialization with functional integration.\\\",\n        \\\"Alpha-band attention research describes suppressive modulation as primarily cortico-cortical, involving frontal and parietal networks, with possible thalamo-cortical contributions when distracting sensory processing must be reduced.\\\",\n        \\\"A cautious synthesis is that conscious access and attentional suppression both depend on organized interactions among specialized cortical systems, while the provided evidence does not establish alpha oscillations as a direct measure of integrated information or consciousness.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-consciousness-corresponds-to-a-system-s-capacity-to-integrate-information-becaus--ca44bbf79dcb\\\",\n        \\\"claim-a-complex-is-an-integrated-subset-with-greater-than-zero-that-is-not-contained-i--70401a6fb458\\\",\n        \\\"claim-a-distributed-thalamocortical-network-is-well-suited-to-generate-consciousness-b--571db463385d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-anatomical-or-functional-disconnection-within-thalamocortical-systems-can-reduce--89adceb072c5\\\",\n        \\\"claim-reticular-sensory-afferent-motor-efferent-and-subcortical-loop-activity-can-modu--173db43834c9\\\",\n        \\\"claim-attention-related-alpha-modulation-appears-primarily-controlled-by-cortico-corti--1eb91088cf2b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alpha-band-oscillations-can-be-actively-invoked-in-cortical-regions-that-process--09466b39d396\\\",\n        \\\"claim-higher-naturally-occurring-or-experimentally-induced-alpha-power-reduces-visual--3884cfa09119\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-03-the-role-of-alpha-band-brain-oscillations-as-a-sensory-suppression-mechanism-dur-w2005105933--7b6b7d5bc8b9\\\",\n        \\\"source-01-an-information-